        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add initial @codebuff/sdk package with CodebuffClient stub",
        "summary": "Introduced @codebuff/sdk v1.0.0 as a private workspace package. Includes CodebuffClient class with newChat and continueChat methods returning empty Context objects. Auth token resolution supports direct string or CODEBUFF_API_KEY env var. Wired into root tsconfig paths and workspace config.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T11:27:53.089Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The team has laid the first bricks for letting external tools talk to Codebuff: they added a new, empty connector kit that other software can import to start chats and continue existing conversations with Codebuff. Right now this connector is private and unfinished, so nothing is using it yet; it only knows how to hand out placeholder results and read an API key passed directly or via an environment variable. If you are building an integration and imported this kit today, you would get back empty conversation responses until the real logic is filled in. This is in place but does nothing yet.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "882873c3d4a9",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:07:21.211Z"
