      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Agents pin subagent versions via shared constant",
        "summary": "Agent configs in `.agents/` now import a shared `version` constant from `.agents/version.ts` to explicitly pin subagent dependencies. Bare string references like `'file-picker'` were replaced with fully qualified, versioned identifiers such as `codebuff/file-picker@${version}`. This change applies to core agents including `base`, `ask`, `brainstormer`, and `charles`, adding `publisher: 'codebuff'` to their metadata. The update ensures spawnable agent versions are validated and consistent across the codebase.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T11:27:54.377Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you use an AI coding assistant, it can call on smaller helper AIs (subagents) to do specific tasks like picking files or exploring a project. The system now makes sure every main assistant explicitly requests a specific, agreed-upon version of those helpers by name and number, rather than just saying 'give me the file picker' with no version pinned. This means the helpers the assistants use are predictable and consistent, so today's assistants will reliably spawn the same version of their subagents that the team tested them with. If you looked at how the assistants are configured, you'd see each one now lists its helpers with a shared version tag and identifies itself as published by Codebuff, instead of each listing helpers by plain names.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "c5d24a0241f7",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:07:22.671Z"
      },
