      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Centralize agent publisher and version in constants",
        "summary": "Refactored agent configuration to import `publisher` and `version` from a new shared `.agents/constants.ts` file, replacing hardcoded strings and the deprecated `.agents/version.ts`. This change affects all agent definitions (e.g., `ask.ts`, `base.ts`, `planner.ts`) by standardizing metadata sources.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T11:28:03.814Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you use one of the project's coding assistants, you'll notice nothing changed on the surface, because the assistant still shows up with the same publisher and version label it always has. Behind the scenes, that label used to be copied and pasted into nearly every assistant's settings file by hand, so the team gathered those duplicate copies into one shared file that all the assistants pull from instead. This means future updates to the publisher or version will only need to be made once, and the old separate file for the version has been retired. The consolidation touches all the built-in assistants, but because the values themselves didn't change, your experience stays exactly the same.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "bc201f0593be",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:07:15.316Z"
      },
